{"name":"Cardamom","hex":"#aaaa77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cardamom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An herb, native to India (Elettaria cardamomum).","Seed of Elettaria cardamomum, used as a medicine and spice, especially in curry powder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cardamom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cardamom","blocks":[{"text":"Cardamom, sometimes cardamon or cardamum, is a spice made from the seeds of several plants in the genera Elettaria and Amomum in the family Zingiberaceae. Both genera are native to the Indian subcontinent and Indonesia. They are recognized by their small seed pods: triangular in cross-section and spindle-shaped, with a thin, papery outer shell and small, black seeds; Elettaria pods are light green and smaller, while Amomum pods are dark brown and larger."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/02017_0119_Kardamom%2C_Winter_in_den_Beskiden.jpg/330px-02017_0119_Kardamom%2C_Winter_in_den_Beskiden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardamom","wikidata":"Q14625808"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Elettaria_cardamomum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-057.jpg/330px-Elettaria_cardamomum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-057.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Elettaria_cardamomum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-057.jpg/330px-Elettaria_cardamomum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-057.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"True cardamom plant (Elettaria cardamomum)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElettaria_cardamomum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-057.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/C